Tue Nov 24 13:23:08 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package a2a-serve 0.1.0 (first upstream release):
  * Serve opencode, Claude Code, or any ACP coding agent as
    a sandboxed A2A agent, one per project directory
  * Config in .a2a/config.yaml, secrets handling, Docker
    sandbox, and `a2a-serve doctor --fix`
  * MCP servers and skills, recipes, schedules, encrypted
    backups, and shell completion
  * Approvals from client, chat, or inspector; identities
    with pairing codes; Google email sign-in
  * Networks over Tailscale, relays, or public URL;
    Telegram, Discord, email; voice via OpenAI, Gemini
  * Agent-to-agent calls and webhook nodes with
    server-held credentials
- Ship the single upstream binary a2a-serve (no sidecar
  in v0.1.0; it appears only on main later)
- Re-gzip vendored tailscale htmx assets (upstream misses
  gzip trailer; JS bytes unchanged, now scanner-clean)

